      "refersTo": "cue-local",
      "description": "Static component sample; runtime number/ring come only from the authoritative deadline.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-cue\"><span class=\"ds-clock\" role=\"timer\" aria-label=\"30 seconds remaining\">30</span><span><strong>Your turn</strong><small>Match green or 7</small></span></div>",
      "css": ".ds-cue{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;min-height:64px;padding:10px 20px 10px 12px;border-radius:18px;background:var(--club-yellow,#ffd45a);color:#38290c;box-shadow:inset 0 -3px 0 #bf8a2860,0 8px 16px #061e4c35;font-family:var(--font-body,Outfit),sans-serif;pointer-events:none}.ds-clock{display:grid;place-items:center;width:44px;height:44px;border:3px solid currentColor;border-radius:50%;font-size:16px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-cue strong{display:block;font-size:18px;font-weight:750;line-height:1.1}.ds-cue small{display:block;margin-top:3px;color:#5a410f;font-size:12px;line-height:1.2}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Color play",
    "overview": "A welcoming shared card table combines a rich blue field, warm cream foreground, vivid native UNO cards and expressive illustrated human portraits. Outfit keeps the interface friendly and direct; Barlow Condensed gives the deck, wordmark and selected game actions their familiar energy. Soft contact shadows and inset press edges make cards and controls feel physical.\n\nThis records the shipped October 24 composite: Classic supplies the blue field and card prominence, Color court supplies the portraits, and After-hours supplies amber turn and action emphasis. The approved direction is `.impeccable/review/experience-reset/contract.md` (FORM seed `2fba311c`); its three references are `reset-classic.png`, `reset-color-court.png` and `reset-after-hours.png` under `.impeccable/mocks/decision/`. No catalog quality-bar world was selected. Earlier Comic-card showdown, giant-cast/painted-menu, violet-corner, illustrated-room and poker-table instructions are historical and superseded. Their assets and provenance remain recoverable; they are not current surface guidance.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Quiet blue or plum preset fields keep attention on live cards and people.",
      "Human portraits, opaque nameplates and exact hand counts make the table social and readable.",
      "Outfit UI and Barlow Condensed deck lettering share one friendly voice.",
      "Amber pressed actions and a compact real countdown explain the current decision.",
      "A bottom-cropped curved hand preserves direct legal play and independent large-hand scrolling."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Published Color Rule",
        "body": "Amber, cream active badges, legal-card outlines and wild swatches describe actual published state. Retain names, counts and written action/color labels alongside color.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Lettering Roles Rule",
        "body": "Outfit carries ordinary interface headings. Condensed italic lettering belongs to brand/deck expression and the existing emphatic game actions; it is not a global heading transform.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Hand Owns Its Width Rule",
        "body": "Large hands scroll inside their own fan; do not shrink them into an unreadable row or allow document-width overflow.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Contact Rule",
        "body": "Use inset press depth for actions and stock/contact depth for cards. Preserve readable resting geometry and keyboard focus; sound and animation never determine turn timing.",
        "section": "elevation & depth"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** use the quiet preset field, warm cream, human portraits and vivid native deck as one shared identity.",
      "**Do** keep Outfit ordinary headings and the separate Barlow Condensed brand/deck roles.",
      "**Do** retain saved supporting appearances and the explicit light native-dialog scope.",
      "**Do** keep exact hand counts, inline compact status, a real turn clock and written action/color cues.",
      "**Do** preserve the curved bottom-held fan, independent overflow, direct legal play and visible keyboard focus.",
      "**Do** use soft contact depth and the intentional inset amber pressed-control lip.",
      "**Do** keep original artwork and exact provenance, even when earlier artwork is superseded.",
      "**Do** verify six-seat landscape phones, large hands and reduced motion when extending the interface."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** restore giant background cast, painted menu-card actions, ink swashes, poker felt/rail or the giant orbit field.",
      "**Don't** add decoration behind the piles or allow compact player states to expand into their space.",
      "**Don't** add another font family, glyph icons, mixed display systems or a parallel component library.",
      "**Don't** replace the live deadline with a decorative countdown or reset it after a draw or metadata update.",
      "**Don't** add blocking splashes or let audio, reactions or motion gate game turns.",
      "**Don't** label No Mercy, Flip or Flex playable before their actual decks/actions exist."
    ]
  }
}
